{"rawEmail":"{\"date\":\"2026-03-30T14:06:16.886Z\",\"subject\":\"Fwd:\",\"text\":\"---------- Forwarded message ---------\\nDe : Yael Favre <yaelfavre22@gmail.com>\\nDate: lun. 30 mars 2026 à 16:04\\nSubject:\\nTo: <2u6idvmpcyvee3z2dwreqly87o44qnfc@hook.eu1.make.com>\\n\\n\\nThe rain fell in a steady, rhythmic whisper against the windowpane,\\nblurring the city lights into smudges of gold and crimson. Inside the small\\ncafé, the world felt suspended in a warm, amber glow. The scent of freshly\\nground coffee beans mingled with the quiet murmur of conversations and the\\nsoft hiss of the espresso machine.\\n\\nEleanor sat by the window, her fingers wrapped around a porcelain cup that\\nhad long since gone cold. She wasn’t drinking anymore; she was watching.\\nAcross the street, a man in a worn trench coat struggled with a stubborn\\numbrella, a small, silent comedy playing out against the grey backdrop of\\nthe afternoon. A moment later, a young woman ran to him, laughing, and they\\ndisappeared together into the shelter of a doorway.\\n\\nEleanor smiled. It was a small thing, a fleeting act of connection in the\\nvastness of the city, yet it felt significant. Here, among strangers\\nseeking refuge from the storm, she was reminded that even on the greyest\\ndays, life pulsed with small, hopeful gestures. She signaled the waiter for\\na fresh cup, ready to sit a while longer and simply watch the world go by.\\n\",\"html\":\"<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><br><br><div class=\\\"gmail_quote gmail_quote_container\\\"><div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" class=\\\"gmail_attr\\\">---------- Forwarded message ---------<br>De : <b class=\\\"gmail_sendername\\\" dir=\\\"auto\\\">Yael Favre</b> <span dir=\\\"auto\\\">&lt;<a href=\\\"mailto:yaelfavre22@gmail.com\\\">yaelfavre22@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span><br>Date: lun. 30 mars 2026 à 16:04<br>Subject: <br>To:  &lt;<a href=\\\"mailto:2u6idvmpcyvee3z2dwreqly87o44qnfc@hook.eu1.make.com\\\">2u6idvmpcyvee3z2dwreqly87o44qnfc@hook.eu1.make.com</a>&gt;<br></div><br><br><div dir=\\\"ltr\\\">\\n<p><span>The rain fell in a steady, \\nrhythmic whisper against the windowpane, blurring the city lights into \\nsmudges of gold and crimson. Inside the small café, the world felt \\nsuspended in a warm, amber glow. The scent of freshly ground coffee \\nbeans mingled with the quiet murmur of conversations and the soft hiss \\nof the espresso machine.</span></p><p><span>Eleanor\\n sat by the window, her fingers wrapped around a porcelain cup that had \\nlong since gone cold. She wasn’t drinking anymore; she was watching. \\nAcross the street, a man in a worn trench coat struggled with a stubborn\\n umbrella, a small, silent comedy playing out against the grey backdrop \\nof the afternoon. A moment later, a young woman ran to him, laughing, \\nand they disappeared together into the shelter of a doorway.</span></p><p><span>Eleanor\\n smiled. It was a small thing, a fleeting act of connection in the \\nvastness of the city, yet it felt significant. Here, among strangers \\nseeking refuge from the storm, she was reminded that even on the greyest\\n days, life pulsed with small, hopeful gestures. She signaled the waiter\\n for a fresh cup, ready to sit a while longer and simply watch the world\\n go by.</span></p>\\n\\n<br></div>\\n</div></div>\\n\",\"from\":{\"address\":\"yaelfavre22@gmail.com\",\"name\":\"Yael Favre\"},\"to\":[{\"address\":\"2u6idvmpcyvee3z2dwreqly87o44qnfc@hook.eu1.make.com\",\"name\":\"\"}],\"cc\":[],\"bcc\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"headers\":{\"received\":\"by mail-oa1-f41.google.com with SMTP id 586e51a60fabf-4138136f02eso2944140fac.2 for <2u6idvmpcyvee3z2dwreqly87o44qnfc@hook.eu1.make.com>; Mon, 30 Mar 2026 07:06:16 -0700 (PDT)\",\"arc-seal\":\"i=1; a=rsa-sha256; t=1774879575; cv=none; d=google.com; s=arc-20240605; b=GYx1kZpdThH8IYZRZeJs6vvLZNiXtcyXrFx6Cl0/hMFzkAG3ryECaDYhz05O20xmYJ TYEZ9BlM1r1KrjyAXr33qnIVNCdz+81YdtxmepR/G5ADd9qJizOQvUMt8VhKz8iC5MBp +umBQzwZYf8EO9o24j1HK3w4+AZwqekXc1aVSGEhMwpWTzMs1ZzjMfrKieXA2jcKIj8t